    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 12,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "My mom and dad say this never happened. They say stuff like \"the imagination of a lonely kid\" and \"young kids can't tell fantasy from reality.\" But I swear a solemn oath: that's a lot of crap. It happened."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 12,
        "line": 938,
        "text": "Sometimes I figure maybe it was just my imagination. It was a long time ago now. I mean at least a. year. Even though he doesn't remember either, my brother, Hakim, believes it happened. If it happened. I like to think it did."
      }
    },
